    "body": "This is definitely misplaced. I'm wondering what it is redundant with? Maybe it would make more sense to move some version of it into the definition of origins?\r\n\r\nThat is, I don't think any specs currently explain why the same origin model is important for preventing information leaking and information spoofing, or how the origin model does not protect against same-origin content (\"cross-directory attacks\").\r\n\r\nAlso, I think it might be worth retaining a warning sentence or two about how these features are available in non-secure contexts, despite that being dangerous.",
